  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Zambia Country Programme works to transform Zambia from a landlocked country into a land-linked trade hub by adopting an integrated corridor approach along the Dar es Salaam, North-South, and Beira corridors, operating since 2020 alongside an economy where mining dominates export earnings but agriculture employs the majority of the population. The Programme&apos;s flagship physical infrastructure investment is the Nakonde OSBP upgrade, a critical gateway on the Dar es Salaam Corridor, where chronic clearance delays exceeding 60 hours are being addressed through new access roads, buildings, ICT systems, and a drive-through cargo scanner, complemented by the already-operational Mchinji&#x2013;Mwami OSBP with Malawi, the first bilateral OSBP in Zambia&apos;s history, officially launched in December 2022. Underpinning these physical investments, the Programme advances digital customs reform through ASYCUDA upgrades, a Single Window, smart gate installation at Kasumbalesa, and cross-border data exchange with Tanzania, Mozambique, Zimbabwe, and South Africa; strengthens SPS and standards capacity including an upgraded phytosanitary laboratory at Nakonde; supports critical raw materials and agricultural value chain export competitiveness through standards and testing improvements; and promotes inclusive trade for small-scale cross-border traders, particularly women.</narrative>
  </description>
